error[type.binding]: `n` declares `int`, this is `int?`
  ╭─[<case>/src/main.av:3:14]
3 │ let n: int = f?.()
  ·              ┬
  ·              ╰── this is `int?`
──╯
help: `f?.()` may be null — `f?.() ?? <default>` supplies a value, `if let n? = f?.() { … } else { … }` branches, and `!` asserts presence
fix (low): assert it is present — `(f?.())!` (traps when it is null)
  (f?.())!
